  "snippet": "#​807 — October 20, 2026 Read on the Web JavaScript Weekly tsrs: Cloudflare and VoidZero's Rust Port of TypeScript — A Rust port of the Go-based TypeScript 7 compiler, built with some input from the TypeScript team and h...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/nuezexh7haulvsllbugt.jpg",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​807 — October 20, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191736/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0 12px;\"><p>JavaScript Weekly</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191669/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/nuezexh7haulvsllbugt.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191669/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.cloudflare.com\">tsrs: Cloudflare and VoidZero's Rust Port of TypeScript</a></span> — A Rust port of the Go-based TypeScript 7 compiler, built with <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191670/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">some input from the TypeScript team</a> and heading into <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191671/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Oxc</a>. Benchmarks claim up to 8x the speed of TypeScript 7.0 and it runs in WebAssembly. Experimental, but <code>npx tsrs</code> works.</p>\n<p>Chen, Mitropoulos and Nakazawa (Cloudflare / VoidZero) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 Max Schwenk started the port with agents writing the code, and <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191672/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">tells the full tale here</a>, including how it took his company's typecheck from 80 seconds to 7.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191668/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/dc7dffad.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191668/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"link.svix.com\">Send Webhooks from Your TypeScript API in Minutes</a></span> — One typed npm package, one call per event. Svix handles retries, signing, delivery logs, and a portal for your customers, so you don't build any of it. Resend sends 200M+ webhooks a year through it.</p>\n<p>Svix <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191673/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.vlt.io\">Thank You, Deno: Competition Keeps JavaScript Moving</a></span> — Last week we covered <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191674/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Deno joining Cloudflare</a> and the future of the Deno runtime. Deno was valuable, says Darcy, as it (and Bun) made the entire ecosystem better by pushing Node and npm to adopt its best ideas.</p>\n<p>Darcy Clarke (vlt) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191675/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Next.js has patched two critical RCE flaws</a>: one in <code>use cache</code> functions via an <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191676/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">upstream React Server Components bug</a> and one in the image optimizer's SVG handling. Upgrade to 16.4.1 or 15.5.28; a <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191677/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">public PoC</a> is already out.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191678/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Node.js security releases are due tomorrow</a> for the 26.x, 24.x and 22.x lines, with the highest severity issue rated high.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Bun compiling JavaScript ahead-of-time, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191679/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">previewed a few weeks ago</a>, now has <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191680/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">a draft PR</a> to produce binaries with no JIT or bytecode.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>RELEASES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191681/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Node.js v26.12.0 (Current)</a> and <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191682/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">v24.22.0 (LTS)</a> – 26.12 can now synchronously load most ES modules and marks the config file stable; 24.22 gains <code>util.throttle</code> and <code>util.debounce</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191683/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Astro 7.4</a> – Adds a <code>--timings</code> flag for <code>astro build</code> to see where build time is spent, plus experimental parallel prerendering across worker threads.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191684/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">React Router 8.5</a> – Deprecates its own view transition APIs in favor of React's &lt;<code>ViewTransition</code>&gt; component, and adds an experimental 'API-only' mode.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191685/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Pretext 1.0</a> – Multiline text layout without touching the DOM. 1.0 ports browsers' own line breakers, so results more closely match what would render.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191686/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">React Native 0.88</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191687/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Elysia 2.0 RC</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191688/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">ESLint 10.13</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191689/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">tsup 9.0</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191690/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Vuetify 4.3</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📖  Articles and Videos</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191691/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"trustsig.eu\">The Tetris Script That Becomes <em>Snake</em> Once Prettified?</a></span> — You'd think pretty-printers and deobfuscators at least leave a script's <em>logic</em> alone, but no. See how chaining semantic quirks in such tools can turn the 'cleaned up' output into a different program!</p>\n<p>Robert Vähhi (TrustSig) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191692/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nolanlawson.com\">Do Web Components Have a Future If Nobody is Writing Them?</a></span> — Nolan has spent years building and defending web components, so this thoughtful, if a little melancholy, piece carries some weight.</p>\n<p>Nolan Lawson </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191693/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"try.expo.dev\">Your CI Was Built for Humans. Your Agents Need Something Else</a></span> — Expo is mobile AI infrastructure. Your agents build, test and ship iOS and Android apps in the background.</p>\n<p>Expo <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\">▶  <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191694/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.youtube.com\">ViteConf 2026: The Full Replay</a></span> — Last week's ViteConf brought ~30 talks including Evan You's keynote on tooling in the agentic era, plus updates on Vitest 5, Vite DevTools, and a faster parser coming to Oxc. It's 10 hours, but there's a hero with timestamps in the comments.</p>\n<p>ViteConf </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 One of the bigger announcements: <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191695/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Void, the Vite team's full-stack SDK and deploy platform, is now open source</a>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191696/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.bryanpg.com\">How to Gaslight JavaScript Programmers (with Proxies)</a></span> — <code>Proxy</code>, introduced as part of ES6 back in the day, has plenty of practical uses but can also make objects behave in curious, unexpected ways. Complete with live, editable examples.</p>\n<p>Bryan Gillespie </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191697/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nothing-else.blog\">How Miro Moved 70,000 Tests from Jest to Vitest</a></span> — The story of moving ~70,000 tests across an 800-package monorepo to Vitest, with AI agents doing most of the laborious work.</p>\n<p>Sergey Nikitin </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191698/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Upgrading to Zod 4 Cut Our Worker CPU by a Third</a> – A Zod 3 to 4.5 migration at 100 million parses a day. <cite>Chris Arderne</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191699/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Using <code>replace()</code> as an Iterator</a> – An old regex-callback-for-side-effects idiom, benchmarked against alternatives. <cite>Eugene Lazutkin</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191700/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Recursion is DEAD and HTML Killed It</a> – Hands-on with Chromium's experimental <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191701/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Declarative Partial Updates</a> proposal. <cite>Dave Rupert</cite></p>\n<p>📺 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191702/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">NightMonkey: Compiling JavaScript Ahead of Time to WebAssembly</a> – An hour-long VMIL 2026 talk from a Wasmtime engineer. <cite>Chris Fallin</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠 Code &amp; Tools</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191703/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ywzqx0owlyt7kwf7wgrk.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191703/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"maplair.org\">Maplair: A Batteries-Included, Tree-Shakeable Fork of Leaflet</a></span> — Still in alpha since last year, one of Leaflet's contributors has forked it, rolling in the 2.0 work plus rotation, fullscreen, search, heatmaps and more – all tree-shakeable.</p>\n<p>Simon Legner </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 The same day, Leaflet's creator <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191704/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">posted a candid update</a> about his experiences living in Ukraine and a plan to get Leaflet 2.0 released.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191707/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"playground.developers.thinkfree.com\">Embeddable DOCX, XLSX &amp; PPTX Editor for Users and AI</a></span> — Let your AI edit existing files via object-level APIs. Users review and keep editing the same file. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191708/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Try Playground</a>.</p>\n<p>Thinkfree <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><span>📊</span> <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191705/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"chartist.dev\">Chartist 2.0: The Lightweight SVG Charting Library Returns</a></span> — A CSS-styled SVG charting library from 2014 that <em>\"went stale over the last years\"</em> makes a comeback with a composable API, server-side rendering to SVG, terminal charts, and still ~12KB gzipped for a line chart. There's <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191706/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">a migration guide</a> for 1.x users.</p>\n<p>Gion Kunz et al. </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191709/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"pele.run\">Pele: Mermaid Diagrams as Lightweight, Themeable SVG</a></span> — Zero-dependency renderer for the Mermaid diagram syntax with responsive layouts and SVG you can theme with CSS variables. Around a sixth the size of Mermaid.js. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191710/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Try the playground</a>.</p>\n<p>Steph Ango (Obsidian) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191711/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/anvwoxijoc5lx7t5nnkh.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191711/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"rich-input.netlify.app\"><code>&lt;rich-input&gt;</code>: A Rich Input Field with GitHub-Style Search Filters</a></span> — A web component for GitHub-style search boxes: free text mixed with autocompleted <code>key:value</code> filters, highlighted in place.</p>\n<p>Bramus Van Damme </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191712/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Chokidar 6.0</a> – The file watcher behind much of JS tooling. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191713/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Rewritten to check changes against the disk before reporting</a> to avoid stray events after a burst of edits, say.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191714/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Happy DOM 21.0</a> – Headless browser environment in pure JavaScript, popular for testing. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191715/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Now blocks stylesheet and <code>iframe</code> loading by default</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191716/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">p-queue 10.0</a> – Promise queue with concurrency control. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191717/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Now dependency-free</a> and an <code>EventTarget</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191718/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Paper.js 0.13</a> and <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191719/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">0.14</a> – Vector graphics scripting framework for canvas. First notable releases in years. (<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191720/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Homepage</a> with <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191721/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">demos</a>.)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🕹️ <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191722/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">LittleJS 1.27</a> – Dependency-free HTML5 game engine that now does 3D too.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🖼️ <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191723/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Skia Canvas 4.0</a> – Canvas API for Node, built on Skia.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>🕵️ Muse doesn’t announce itself. Meta’s AI agent browses like a real user. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191724/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">See how Fingerprint detects it</a> by name and try free for yourself.</p>\n<p>🎬 Your app needs video, not a video team. Upload any format to <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191725/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Hyperserve's API</a>, get back MP4 on a global CDN. Ship video in an afternoon.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191726/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/t1yy7vc2vsopynkoyvrc.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>🖼️ <strong>JPEG XL:</strong> The modern image format is now supported by all major browsers, with <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191727/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Firefox 158</a> the latest to enable it by default. Jake Archibald <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191728/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">pits it against AVIF in this extensive review</a>. What I find amazing is <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191726/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">what it's able to render in under 100 bytes</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>NodeConf EU 2026:</strong> The <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191729/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">▶️ latest NodeConf EU talks</a> are up, including James Snell's case for <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191730/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">a common minimum API every runtime should support</a>, plus sessions on <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191731/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">V8 heap management</a> and <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191732/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Emscripten and WebAssembly</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>A new social network:</strong> <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191733/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">/dev/null</a> is a GitHub-oriented social network for developers, built from scratch in 48 hours. It already has over 8000 members, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/191734/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">including me</a>. It's been a lot of fun so far!</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
